$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM In a pressure vial containing 22 (970 mg, 2.22 mmol) was added
5-(prop-1-yn-1-yl)pyridin-3-yl boronic acid (536 mg, 3.33 mmol), 2 M
Na2CO3 (1.22 mL, 2.44 mmol) and dioxane (7.4 mL). The resultant mixture
was degassed by bubbling N2 through it for 5 min. To the mixture was then
added PdCl2(dppf)-CH2Cl2 (181 mg, 0.222 mmol). The vial was purged with
nitrogen, sealed and placed into a preheated oil bath at 65°C. The
mixture was stirred at that temperature for 4 hours. The mixture was then
allowed to cool to room temperature, partitioned between brine and EtOAc
followed by filtration through a pad of Celite. The aqueous layer was
extracted with EtOAc (3x). The combined organic layers were dried over
Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated. The crude product was purified via
flash chromatography (SiO2; gradient elution 100:0 to 60:40
hexanes:EtOAc) to afford the intermediate carbamate. Light yellow solid,
yield 660 mg, 1.395 mmol, 62.8 %. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 10.47 (brs,
1H), 8.56 (s, 1H), 8.48 (s, 1H), 7.68 (s, 1H), 7.09 (s, 1H), 3.59 (d, J =
16.4, 1H), 3.21 (s, 3H), 2.80 (d, J = 16.4 Hz, 1H), 2.05 (s, 3 H), 1.82
(s, 3H), 1.51 (s, 9H). MS (ESI): m/z 473.2 [M+H]+, 495.2 [M+Na]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, pressure vial used and sealed, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of an Orally Available, Brain Penetrant BACE1 Inhibitor That
Affords Robust CNS Aβ Reduction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
