$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound (4T-1): From 6a: To a degassed solution of 6a (63.2 mg, 0.118
mmol), 3a (105.7 mg, 0.281 mmol, 2.4 equiv) in distilled THF (7 mL) was
added Pd2dba3 (11.2 mg, 10 mol%), Cs2CO3 (162.0 mg, 0.497 mmol, 4.2
equiv) and P(t-Bu)3 (0.05 mL, 40 mol%). The reaction medium was stirred
at 30 °C for 15 h. The reaction was quenched with H2O, extracted with
CH2Cl2, washed with water, dried with brine and over Na2SO4. Purification
on a silica column chromatography using CH2Cl2/petroleum ether (30/70) as
eluent, followed by recrystallization from CH2Cl2/EtOH afforded the
desired product. Yield: 56.7 mg, 62%, red metallic needles. 1H NMR (400
MHz, CD2Cl2): δ (ppm) = 0.90 (t, 6H, 3J = 7.0 Hz), 1.30-1.43 (m, 12H),
1.67 (qt, 4H, 3J = 7.7 Hz), 2.47 (s, 3H), 2.81 (t, 4H, 3J = 7.6 Hz), 6.75
(d, 2H, 3J = 3.6 Hz), 6.89 (s, 2H), 6.94 (d, 2H, 3J = 3.5 Hz), 7.12 (d,
2H, 3J = 5.3 Hz), 7.286 (d, 2H, 3J = 5.2 Hz), 7.293 (d, 2H, 3J = 8.1 Hz),
7.43 (d, 2H, 3J = 8.1 Hz), 7.88 (s, 2H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CD2Cl2): δ
(ppm) = 14.4, 21.8, 23.2, 29.4, 30.8, 32.1, 32.3, 125.0, 125.5, 128.3,
128.6, 128.97, 129.07, 129.12, 129.7, 131.3, 131.4, 131.5, 132.3, 132.8,
135.5, 142.2, 143.7, 147.0, 148.6. 11B NMR (128.4 MHz, CD2Cl2): δ (ppm) =
0.03 (t, JB-F = 28.8 Hz). EI-MS (m/z, relative intensity): theoretical
mass 778.25 (100); found 778.1 (100), 759.1 (35). Anal. calcd for
C44H45BF2N2S4 (Mr = 778.25): C, 67.85; H, 5.82; N, 3.60. Anal. found: C,
67.62; H, 5.64; N, 3.42. λAbs (nm): 604, ϵ (M-1 · cm-1): 36100, λEm (nm):
680.
