$DATUM Porphyrin 4 (83 mg, 1 equiv), boronic ester 3 (70 mg 1.1 equiv),
Pd(PPh3)4 (6 mg, 0.05 equiv) and Cs2CO3 (65 mg, 2.0 equiv) were dried
under vacuum and then purged with argon. Then degassed toluene (5 mL) and
DMF (2 mL) were added and the mixture was stirred for 36 hours at 96 °C
and after cooling, water was added and the product was extracted with
ethyl acetate (3 × 10 mL). The organic layer was washed with saturated
brine and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was removed under
vacuum and the residue was purified by column chromatography (silica gel,
DCM: hexane = 1:3) to give a brown waxy solid product. Immediately, this
solid was dissolved in CHCl3 (10 mL), and a saturated solution of
Zn(OAc)2 in methanol (3 mL) was added slowly. The mixture was stirred for
3 hours at 50 °C. After removal of the solvents, the crude product was
purified by column chromatography (silica gel, hexane: DCM = 3:1) to give
a yellow solid product 5 (80 mg, 59% in two steps). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500
MHz) δ: 9.62 (d, J= 4.5 Hz, 2H), 9.49 (d, J= 3.2 Hz, 2H), 9.12 (d, J= 5.9
Hz, 2H), 8.94 (d, J= 5.1 Hz, 2H), 8.82 (d, J= 7.6 Hz, 1H), 8.70 (d, J=
7.0 Hz, 2H), 8.37 (d, J= 8.2 Hz, 1H), 8.22 (m, 1H), 8.17 (m, 1H), 8.01
(s, 1H), 7.89-7.92 (m, 2H), 7.85 (d, J= 8.2 Hz, 2H), 7.73 (d, J= 8.2 Hz,
2H), 7.45-7.49 (m, 1H), 7.21-7.23 (m, 1H), 5.13 (m, 2H), 4.75-4.80 (m,
4H), 2.77 (m, 2H), 2.43-2.45 (m, 1H), 0.78-1.82 (m, 73H). 13C NMR (CDCl3,
125 MHz), δ: 151.1, 151.03, 150.93, 150.89, 150.7, 150.1, 149.5, 148.5,
142.2, 139.2, 137.9, 137.4, 133.6, 132.7, 132.3, 132.1, 131.7, 130.8,
