$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A solution of crude boronic acid 15c (ca. 0.75 mmol), sodium carbonate
(33 mg, 0.31 mmol), tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (60 mg,
0.052 mmol) and bromide S1 (110 mg, 0.50 mmol) in DME/water (8/1, 2.0 mL)
was stirred at 110°C under microwave irradiation for 1 h. The reaction
was quenched with brine and extracted with EtOAc. The combined organics
were washed with brine, dried (Na2SO4), concentrated and purified by
Biotage column chromatography (0-15% MeOH/DCM). Pyridine 16k (115 mg,
58%). Methyl
4-(2-amino-5-(4-((dimethylamino)methyl)thiophen-2-yl)pyridin-3-yl)-2-methoxybenzoate
16k HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C21H24N3O3S (M + H) 398.1533, found
398.1530. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.37 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H), 7.91 (d, J
= 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.61 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H), 7.21 (d, J = 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.12
(dd, J = 7.9, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.09 (s, 1H), 7.04 (s, 1H), 4.70 (s, 2H), 3.96
(s, 3H), 3.94 (s, 3H), 2.30 (s, 6H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (in stage 1), Suzuki coupling
