$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7: Potassium
6-Fluoro-4-oxo-8-(1,3,5-trimethyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-4H-chromene-2-carboxylate.
A slurry of ethyl 8-bromo-6- fluoro-4-oxo-4H-chromene-2-carboxylate (1.24
g, 3.93 mmol),
1,3,5-trimethyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole
(1.23 g, 5.21 mmol), bis(triphenylphosphine)-palladium(II) chloride (276
mg, 0.39 mmol), potassium carbonate (1.63 g, 11.8 mmol), DME (50 mL),
water (21 mL), and ethanol (14 mL) was vacuum degassed (three cycles) and
then heated to 90 °C for 16 h. Reaction was cooled to room temperature
and filtered through Celite. Solids were washed with DME (3 x 20 mL), and
filtrate was evaporated. DME was added (30 mL) and evaporated (3x) to
azeotrope water. This solid was suspended in 50 mL of DME, filtered,
washed with more DME, and dried under high vacuum for 3 h. The pink crude
solid potassium salt was typically carried on in further reactions
without purification (0.66 g, 58%).
6-Fluoro-4-oxo-8-(1,3,5-trimethyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-4H-chromene-2-carboxylate,
yield (0.66 g, 58%). LC/MS 0.82min, m/z 317 (M + H); 1H NMR(300 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ ppm 2.13 (s, 3 H), 2.23 (s, 3 H), 3.74 (s, 3 H), 6.68 (s, 1
H), 7.51 (dd, J=9.0, 2.8 Hz, 1 H), 7.57-7.77 (m, 1 H).
