$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
3-(5-Ethoxy-6-(1-methyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-1H-indazol-3-yl)-benzenesulfonamide
(23c). A mixture of compound 22a (30 mg, 0.060 mmol),
1-methylpyrazole-4-boronic acid pinacol ester (18.9 mg, 0.091 mmol),
Pd(OAc)2 (1.40 mg, 6.2 μmol), S-Phos (4.96 mg, 0.12 mmol), and aqueous 2
M K2CO3 (121 μL, 0.242 mmol) in THF (1 mL) was heated to reflux for 5 h.
The mixture was allowed to cool to room temperature and diluted with H2O
and EtOAc. The aqueous layer was separated and extracted with EtOAc. The
combined organic extracts were washed with H2O and brine, dried over
MgSO4, filtered, and evaporated to give Boc protected 23c. To a solution
of this compound in DCM (0.5 mL) was added TFA (0.5 mL). The mixture was
stirred at room temperature and diluted with DCM and 10% aqueous K2CO3
solution. The aqueous layer was separated and extracted with EtOAc. The
combined organic extracts were washed with H2O and brine, dried over
MgSO4, filtered, and evaporated. The residue was purified by flash
chromatography (silica gel; CHCl3/ MeOH, gradient, 3−10% MeOH).
3-(5-(Cyclohexyloxy)-6-(1-methyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-1H-indazol-3-yl)benzenesulfonamide
(23f). Compound 23f was prepared in a manner similar to that for 23c in
56% yield (37.8 mg). 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 1.28−1.75 (m, 8H),
1.99−2.06 (m, 2H), 3.90 (s, 3H), 4.50−4.58 (m, 1H), 7.47 (s, 2H), 7.50
(s, 1H), 7.69−7.74 (m, 2H), 7.81 (d, J =7.1 Hz, 1H), 7.97 (s, 1H),
8.16−8.19 (m, 2H), 8.42 (s, 1H), 13.22 (s, 1H). LRMS-ESI (m/z): [M + H]+
calcd for C23H26N5O3S, 452; found, 452.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Indazole-Based Potent and Cell-Active Mps1 Kinase Inhibitors: Rational
Design from Pan-Kinase Inhibitor Anthrapyrazolone (SP600125)
