$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: METHOD L: SUZUKI-TYPE CROSS-COUPLING OF ALKYL
BROMIDES Modified from a procedure reported by Fu.14 In a glove box,
Ni(cod)2 (0.10 equiv.), bathophenanthroline (BPhen, 0.20 equiv.),
anhydrous KOt-Bu (1.6 equiv.), arylboronic acid (1.2 equiv.), and freshly
distilled s-butanol (3.0 mL) were added to a flame dried 7 mL vial
equipped with a stir bar and stirred at ambient temperature for 10 min.
Substrate (1.0 equiv.) was added to the reaction vial, which was then
capped with a septum and removed from the glove box. The reaction vial
was put under N2 in a 60 °C oil bath. After stirring for 24 h, the
reaction was allowed to cool to ambient temperature before it was passed
through a silica gel plug (50% Et2O/hexanes). The filtrate was
concentrated in vacuo. cis-(±)-2-(2-Naphthyl)-4-phenyl-tetrahydropyran
(cis-21) was also prepared according to Method L. The following amounts
of reagents were used: Ni(cod)2 (5.9 mg, 0.020 mmol, 0.040 equiv.),
bathophenanthroline (13 mg, 0.040 mmol, 0.080 equiv.), anhydrous KOt-Bu
(89 mg, 0.80 mmol, 1.6 equiv.), phenylboronic acid (74 mg, 0.60 mmol, 1.2
equiv.), s-butanol (3.0 mL) and substrate 22 (140 mg, 0.50 mmol, 1.0
equiv.). The compound was purified by flash column chromatography
(5-20-50% EtOAc/hexanes).
cis-(±)-6-(2-(Naphthyl)-tetrahydropyranyl)-2,3-dihydrobenzo[b][1,4]dioxine
(cis-29) was prepared according to Method L. The following amounts of
reagents were used: Ni(cod)2 (14 mg, 0.050 mmol, 0.10 equiv.),
bathophenanthroline (33 mg, 0.10 mmol, 0.20 equiv.), anhydrous KOt-Bu
(90. mg, 0.80 mmol, 1.6 equiv.), 1,4-benzodioxane-6-boronic acid (110 mg,
0.60 mmol, 1.2 equiv.), s-butanol (3.0 mL) and substrate 22 (150 mg, 0.50
mmol, 1.0 equiv.). The compound was purified by flash column
chromatography (5% Et2O/hexanes). The title compound as a faintly pink
oil (95 mg, 0.27 mmol, 55%, dr >20:1). The dr was determined based on
integration of the benzylic methines in the 1H NMR spectrum. The relative
configuration was assigned as cis by COSY and NOE NMR experiments.
Irradiation of the benzylic proton (HA) gave an NOE enhancement of 2.1%
of HC, an enhancement of 3.3% of HD, and an enhancement of 2.1% of HE.
TLC Rf = 0.2 (5% Et2O/hexanes); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.84-7.80 (m,
4H), 7.49 (dd, J = 8.6, 1.3, 1H), 7.47-7.42 (m, 2H), 6.82-6.77 (m, 2H),
6.73 (dd, J = 8.3, 1.9, 1H), 4.62 (dd, J = 11.1, 1.1, 1H), 4.32 (ddd, J =
11.5, 3.7, 2.0, 1H), 4.22 (s, 4H), 3.80 (td, J = 11.1, 3.6, 1H),
2.94-2.88 (m, 1H), 2.14 (add, J = 13.2, 2.0, 1H), 1.91-1.84 (m, 2H), 1.78
(q, J = 12.2, 1H); 13C NMR(125.7 MHz, CDCl3) δ 143.6, 142.1, 140.3,
139.1, 133.5, 133.0, 128.1, 127.8, 126.1, 125.8, 124.5, 124.4, 119.8,
117.3, 115.6, 80.1, 68.9, 64.54, 64.45, 41.7, 41.5, 33.7; IR (neat) 2933,
1508, 1284, 1068 cm-1; HRMS (TOF MS ES+) m / z calcd for C23H22O3Na (M +
Na)+ 369.1467, found 369.1469.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Suzuki-type cross-coupling, dr >20:1, glove box used in
stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereospecific Cross-Coupling Reactions of Aryl-Substituted
Tetrahydrofurans, Tetrahydropyrans, and Lactones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tollefson, Emily J.; Dawson, David D.; Osborne, Charlotte A.; Jarvo,
Elizabeth R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2014), 136(42), 14951-14958

