$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure B: Suzuki couplings of
6-bromo-4-[(2-ethylbutyl)amino]-3- quinolinecarboxamide 26 with
arylboronic acid/esters; Synthesis of analogues 27-29 A mixture of
6-bromo-4-[(2-ethylbutyl)amino]-3-quinolinecarboxamide 26 (1 equiv.), the
desired boronic acid/ester (1.1 equiv.), cesium carbonate (2.5 equiv.)
and tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium (0.04 equiv.) in dioxane/water
(1:1) was degassed and sealed into a microwave tube. The reaction was
heated to 150 °C for 30 minutes in a microwave reactor and cooled to RT.
The crude product was purified by preparative LCMS, using decreasingly
polar mixtures of water (containing 1% NH3) and MeCN as eluents.
Fractions containing the desired compound were evaporated to dryness. The
desired compounds.
4-[(2-Ethylbutyl)amino]-6-(4-pyridinyl)-3-quinolinecarboxamide (27)
General procedure B was applied to afford ethyl
4-(2-ethylbutoxy)-6-(pyridin-3-yl)quinoline-3-carboxylate as an off white
solid (80 mg, 54%). m/z 378 (M+H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, thermal, sealed tube used (microwave), Suzuki
coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Novel 3-Quinoline Carboxamides as Potent, Selective, and
Orally Bioavailable Inhibitors of Ataxia Telangiectasia Mutated (ATM)
Kinase
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
