$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Cross-Coupling
Reactions. To a solution of the aryl halide (1.0 equiv) in 1,4-dioxane,
was added the appropriate boronic acid (1.1 equiv). The mixture was
thoroughly degassed with nitrogen for 15 min, and then Pd(PPh)3Cl2 (5-7
mol %) was added under a nitrogen atmosphere followed by aqueous K2CO3 (1
M, 3.0 equiv). The reaction mixture was stirred at 110 °C for 16 h,
poured into H2O, and extracted with EtOAc (3Å). The combined organic
layers were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated in
vacuo. The residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel
hexane/EtOAc. The product as a solid.
3,5-Bis(6-(trifluoromethyl)pyridin-3-yl)pyrazin-2-amine (32) (54%).
201-203 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.27 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 9.21 (d,
J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 8.62 (s, 1H), 8.44 (m, 1H), 8.42 (m, 1H), 7.87 (d, J =
8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.77 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 6.85 (s, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
DMSO-d6): δ 154.1, 150.2, 147.1, 145.4, 144.6, 140.3, 141.3, 138.5,136.8,
136.4, 135.9, 135.0, 134.3, 123.4, 121.2, 111.2. Anal. RP-HPLC tR = 12.8
min (purity 99.3%). Calculated for C16H9F6N5 385.27, Observed m/z [M+H]+
386.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
