$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-(5-Bromo-2,3-diphenylquinoxalin-8-yl)thiophene-2-carbaldehyde (5). A
mixture of 4 (0.33 g, 0.69 mmol), 5-formyl-2-thiopheneboronic acid (0.11
g, 0.71 mmol) and tetrakis(triphenylphosphine) palladium(0) (0.012 g,
0.01 mmol) was dissolved in 10 ml THF and sodium bicarbonate (0.075 g,
0.71 mmol) in 1 ml water was added. After stirring at 70 °C for 4 h under
argon, the mixture was poured into water and extracted with chloroform.
The organic layers were separated, dried over magnesium sulfate and
filtered. After evaporation of solvent, the residues were subjected to
column chromatography using chloroform to produce 0.19 g (54 %) of 5 as a
yellowish solid. mp 227~228°C. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) = 9.98
(s, 1H), 8.11(d, 1H), 8.02 (d, 1H), 7.90 (d, 12H), 7.81 (d, 1H),
7.68-7.70 (m, 4H), 7.36-7.43 (m, 6H), 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) =
182.3, 152.7, 152.3, 146.5, 144.4, 137.8, 137.0, 136.9, 136.8, 134.5,
131.9, 130.1, 129.3, 129.2, 128.6, 128.5, 127.5, 127.3, 126.4, 124.1.
FT-IR (KBr, ν/cm-1) = 3060, 2821, 1666, 1523, 1444, 1434, 1385, 1332,
1224, 1097, 1060, 978, 813, 772, 696, 538, 506. HR-MS (APCI) calcd for
C25H16N2OSBr, 471.0167 [M+ H]+; found, 470.0168.
