$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Pyridine (568 mg, 7.20 mmol) was added to a
solution of 26 (600 mg, 2.40 mmol), 4-cyanophenylboronic acid (423 mg,
2.88 mmol), and Cu(OAc)2 (1.31 g, 7.20 mmol) in anhydrous DMSO (8 mL).
The resulting mixture was stirred under an oxygen balloon at 40-50 °C for
4 days. The reaction mixture was quenched with water and extracted with
EtOAc. The combined organic layer was filtered through a pad of Celite.
The filtrate was washed with water, brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4,
and concentrated. The residue was purified by silica gel column (nhexane/
EtOAc = 1:1) to give 27f. Compound 27g was prepared according to the
procedure described for the synthesis of 27f using 26 (563 mg, 2.24 mmol)
and 4-methoxy-3-pyridylboronic acid to give 27g (417 mg, 52%).
