$DATUM 7-(1-Cyclopropylmethyl-1H-indol-5-yl)-3-(2,2,2-trifluoroethyl)-imidazo[1,2-a]pyridine-8-carbonitrile
(27g). To a mixture of 6b (0.12 g, 0.39 mmol) and 13g (0.14 g, 0.47 mmol)
in a saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (1 mL) and 1,4-dioxane (1 mL)
was added Pd(PPh3)4 (0.023 g, 0.02 mmol). The mixture was heated at 150
°C for 10 min under microwave irradiation. The mixture was cooled to room
temperature and filtered through a Celite pad. The filtrate was diluted
with water (10 mL) and extracted with EtOAc (2 × 10 mL). The organic
layer was washed with brine (10 mL), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and the
volatiles were evaporated in vacuo. The residue thus obtained was
purified by flash column chromatography (silica gel, MeOH-NH3 in CH2Cl2,
0/100 to 10/90) to give 27g. Yellow solid (0.079 g, 51%). Mp 117.9 °C. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 0.34-0.47 (m, 2H), 0.60-0.74 (m, 2H),
1.24-1.37 (m, 1H), 3.79 (q, J= 9.8 Hz, 2H), 4.04 (d, J= 6.9 Hz, 2H), 6.62
(d, J= 3.2 Hz, 1H), 7.19 (d, J= 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.32 (d, J= 3.2 Hz, 1H),
7.51 (d, J= 8.8 Hz, 1H), 7.56 (dd, J= 8.6, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 7.76 (s, 1H),
7.97-7.99 (m, 1H), 8.19 (d, J= 7.4 Hz, 1H). LC-MS: m/z 395 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, thermal, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Imidazo[1,2-a]pyridines: Orally Active Positive Allosteric Modulators of
the Metabotropic Glutamate 2 Receptor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
